    <string name="ai_help_summary">Simple guide to using the AI safely</string>
    <string name="ai_help_message">The AI Agent can run real commands inside your Termux to get work done.\n\n1. Open \"AI Agent\" from Settings or from the terminal context menu.\n2. Type any task in simple language, e.g. \"install python and run a test script\".\n3. The AI plans shell commands and asks for your approval before every command.\n4. If a command fails, the AI reads the error and tries to fix it (max retries are configurable).\n5. Press Stop any time to cancel everything.\n\nSafety: every command is approved by you first, dangerous commands (like rm -rf) are always flagged, and everything the AI runs is printed in the session log.</string>


